  "summary": "Low key as a term used in describing paintings or photographs is related to but not the same as low-key lighting in cinema or photography.",
  "description": "Low key as a term used in describing paintings or photographs is related to but not the same as low-key lighting in cinema or photography. A photographic image, painting or movie can be defined as \"low-keyly\" if its dominant values are black, dark brown or dark blue.\n\nSome authors describe the term \"low key\" as the so-called Rembrandian light while others describe how to obtain such photographs or paintings.",
